## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design robust multi-tenant data quality controls, handles schema drift, and preserves latency SLAs under backpressure.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant schema catalogs and versioning
- QualityGate operator contracts and DLQ routing
- Backward-compatible schema evolution and drift metrics
- Latency budgeting and backpressure handling
- Canary testing with synthetic tenants

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: QualityGate interface for KCNA
class QualityGate {
  constructor(schemaCatalog){ this.catalog = schemaCatalog }
  validate(event){ const schema = this.catalog.get(event.tenantId, event.version); return schema ? schema.validate(event) : false }
  route(event, valid){ return valid ? event : { error: 'schema-violation' } }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

